// APW-6 — Net open-count window cap (opens minus completed reviews) — CORRECT variant.
//
// Intent: a coding agent may hold at most 3 open pull requests at once. A new
// open is allowed only while fewer than 3 are open, measured as opens minus
// completed reviews in the 24h window; the guard runs before the new PR lands,
// so `< 3` now means at most 3 open afterwards.
//
// The correct / buggy distinction is the event kind of the counted events
// (mirroring the other shapes):
//   * `request`  (CORRECT): counting *requested* opens / reviews -> the net
//     open count is accurate.
//   * `response` (BUGGY):   counting only *settled* opens / reviews -> a
//     denied open or a stalled review distorts the net count (the cap is not
//     enforced reliably).
//
// The `-` between the two counts is the arithmetic: net opens = opens - reviews.
//
// Schema: Repo namespace (cap_open_agent_prs_windowed example).
// See: rot/shapes.py (the count-window oracle, build_count_window_ir).
@id("count_window_correct")
permit (
    principal,
    action == Repo::Action::"OpenPullRequest",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (count for (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 24h (Repo::Action::"OpenPullRequest"::request{} && tp(t))
    ))
    - (count for (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 24h (Repo::Action::"CompleteReview"::request{} && tp(t))
    )) < 3
};